<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation was a movement of Cambodian communists opposed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a>, founded under Vietnamese sponsorship in December 1978. Its leaders, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heng-samrin">Heng Samrin</a>, Chea Sim and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a>, were former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Rouge cadres who had fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. It accompanied the Vietnamese invasion and in January 1979 formed the government of the People's Republic of Kampuchea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kampuchean-united-front-for-national-salvation.jpg" alt="Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FUNSK-emblem.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
